    <!-- What paying a SHA256 invoice means -->
    <string name="send_explainer_title">Paying a SHA256 invoice</string>
    <string name="send_explainer_1">A SHA256 invoice asks to be paid on the SHA256 chain\'s Lightning network. Your node can\'t pay there itself, so a service pays it for you, and you pay the service in BTCB2.</string>
    <string name="send_explainer_2">You don\'t have to trust the service: your payment to it is locked to the same invoice, so it can only collect by paying the SHA256 invoice. If it doesn\'t, your payment comes back to you.</string>
    <string name="send_explainer_3">The price is the service\'s rate and fee. Your node checks it against the market rate, and you agree to the most it can cost before anything is paid.</string>
    <string name="send_explainer_4">It is usually paid within a minute or two. If the service stalls, your payment can stay held until its time runs out, at most about two weeks, and then comes back.</string>
    <string name="send_explainer_5">The service is the one set up in the dashboard, under Paying SHA256 invoices.</string>
    <string name="send_explainer_ok">Got it</string>

